-The severity rows carry a warning for the organisation. Best recall is not on the blockers but on the majors (0.702 against 0.486), because the four blocker rules are precisely the rules whose satisfaction cannot be read off the surface: an authorisation chain that is closed, an encryption scheme that is sound and a rate-limiting policy that is adequate all require a reader. A checklist deployed as keyword checks therefore fails most often on the findings that block a release, which is the empirical form of the verifiability tension.
+Zero false positives is an observed property of these labels and this judge, not a consequence of located evidence. Eighteen of 35 blocker defects are missed. All blocker rules happen to be hybrid in this package; neither that composition nor the recall ordering proves a general severity--verifiability relationship. Seventeen misses occur in hard rules, showing that automatic eligibility can coexist with inadequate proxy predicates.
 
-\subsection{Where the Remaining Misses Are (RQ1)}\label{sec:misses}
+\subsection{Traceability and Pending Workload (RQ3)}\label{sec:misses}
 
-All 85 misses are either planned pending states or a documented limit of decisive verifiers; none is a silent pass on a located defect. Sixty-eight are hybrid defects reported as \emph{pending}---27 absent and 30 hollow phrasings the flag judge cannot decide, plus 11 negated or placeholder spans rejected by the gate---so 80\% of all misses are shown to the expert as open items rather than hidden; a review surfaces 6--13 pending items, median 9. The remaining 17 are hard rules decisive on keyword presence (load-test statement 7, channel identifier 5, change-list table 5) that miss placeholder or hollow phrasings, the documented trade-off for making these rules fully automatic.
-
-Table~\ref{tab:kinds} and Figure~\ref{fig:kinds} separate the mechanism's reach by defect kind, and the contrast with the keyword baseline is the clearest single statement of what typing buys. The keyword baseline finds absence only when the keyword is missing entirely (45 of 98) and essentially nothing of the three other kinds (1 of 37 negated, 0 of 52 placeholder, 1 of 66 hollow)---its apparent capability on absence is also the source of its false positives, because it cannot distinguish ``the keyword is missing because the requirement is unmet'' from ``the keyword is missing because the author used another word''. The typed design moves all four kinds upward, and the ordering that remains---absent 0.72, negated 0.84, placeholder 0.81, hollow 0.36---is the ordering of what structure alone can decide.
+Sixty-eight of 85 missed planted defects occur in pending hybrid document--rule pairs (80\% referral coverage). Seventeen remain unsurfaced by the evaluated automatic routes. Referral is not recovery: the stored result does not show that a reviewer read the item, identified the defect or corrected the verdict. The full pending set contains 932 unique hybrid pairs, mean 9.32 per document, median nine and range 6--13, excluding soft-rule items. Sixty-eight of these 932 pairs match planted defects (7.3\% label density). The other pairs must not be called false positives: a pending item asserts uncertainty, not a defect. Nor is that density a measure of review time, which was not measured.
 
