+Fifteen of 70 policy-non-Pass documents are under-called (21.4\%); ten receive Pass (14.3\%), comprising six expected Revise and four expected Fail. Of 23 expected Fail documents, four receive Pass (17.4\%) and nine receive a non-Fail recommendation (39.1\%). Ten of the 40 suggested Pass recommendations are incorrect against the policy labels (25\%). The 13 genuinely zero-defect documents all have no finding. Seventeen further documents are policy Pass despite minor planted defects. These denominators prevent both inflating ``clean-document'' performance and mistaking all defects on a Pass document for a false clearance.
 
